{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791634897,"nonce":"4M7OmovsNwjyyIOpfE6siGAnbQc=","title":"Ask whether many nodes are in view, sharing the walk to their ancestors","message":"LayoutContext::in_view walks from the root to the node for every call. A host that asks it of every animated node each frame pays that walk per node, though siblings share every ancestor: asked of 2000 siblings each tick it doubled a host's motion tick.\n\nFactor one node of the walk into Tree::step, which Tree::in_view (and through it the HashLink entry point) uses unchanged, and add LayoutContext::view(): a View that keeps what each ancestor leaves its children, so a walk to a shared ancestor is made once per view.","files":null}]}